{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy"]]},"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"coloredNeighbors","kind":"identifier"}]}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"First the vertex of greatest degree (the least index on ties), then repeatedly the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"uncoloured vertex with the most coloured neighbours. Ties among those fall as a two-way"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"indexed binary max-heap breaks them, not by index: vertices are pushed in index order and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"raised neighbour by neighbour in ascending order; an entry moves above an equal parent and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sinks to the left child unless the right one is strictly greater. O((n + m) log n)."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/coloringstrategy\/coloredneighbors"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/coloredNeighbors"},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"ColoringModule"}],"fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"coloredNeighbors","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"s:14ColoringModule0A8StrategyO16coloredNeighborsyA2CmF","roleHeading":"Case","symbolKind":"case","title":"ColoringStrategy.coloredNeighbors","role":"symbol"},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/ColoringStrategy":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ColoringStrategy"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kin